WEBVTT

00:04.650 --> 00:07.150
This is Allen Company training on the Federal Mine

00:07.150 --> 00:10.862
Safety and Health Act of 1977, the law that created

00:10.862 --> 00:14.300
MSHA and the rights you have as a miner.

00:14.300 --> 00:17.312
Part 48 requires that we discuss Section 2 of the

00:17.312 --> 00:20.463
Act, and how supervisors and miners' representatives

00:20.463 --> 00:22.637
fit into safety at the mine.

00:23.748 --> 00:26.498
Section 2 is Congress's statement of why the law

00:26.498 --> 00:29.773
exists. It says the first priority and concern

00:29.773 --> 00:32.810
of everyone in mining must be the health and safety

00:32.810 --> 00:35.761
of its most precious resource: the miner.

00:35.761 --> 00:38.310
It finds that deaths and serious injuries from

00:38.310 --> 00:41.461
unsafe conditions cause grief and suffering and

00:41.461 --> 00:43.723
are a serious drain on the economy.

00:43.723 --> 00:46.560
It says operators, with the help of miners,

00:46.560 --> 00:49.610
have the primary responsibility to prevent unsafe

00:49.610 --> 00:52.185
and unhealthy conditions. And it says there's a

00:52.185 --> 00:55.898
need for mandatory standards, enforced by the government,

00:55.898 --> 00:57.398
to protect miners.

00:58.518 --> 01:01.456
In plain terms: Allen is responsible for providing

01:01.456 --> 01:04.505
a safe mine, and you're part of making it safe.

01:04.505 --> 01:07.393
That means following the rules, reporting hazards,

01:07.393 --> 01:09.543
and stopping work that isn't safe.

01:10.656 --> 01:14.068
At Allen, Hunter Kenney is over all of our sites.

01:14.068 --> 01:16.868
At Boonesboro, the line runs from Hunter Kenney

01:16.868 --> 01:19.631
to Dustin Conn, then to Kendell Barnes.

01:19.631 --> 01:22.931
At Dix River, it's Hunter Kenney, Gene Smith,

01:22.931 --> 01:25.731
then Braden Walters. And at Clover Bottom,

01:25.731 --> 01:28.218
mines one and two, it's Hunter Kenney,

01:28.218 --> 01:30.756
Andrew Burton, then Braden Walters.

01:30.756 --> 01:33.181
From there it runs through your supervisor to you.

01:33.181 --> 01:35.693
Your supervisor is responsible for examining your

01:35.693 --> 01:38.731
work area, assigning tasks you're trained for,

01:38.731 --> 01:41.781
and correcting hazards. The Safety Manager supports

01:41.781 --> 01:42.843
every site.

01:43.962 --> 01:46.174
Know where your supervisor works and how to reach

01:46.174 --> 01:48.612
them. Some offices are on the surface,

01:48.612 --> 01:51.524
and some are underground, like this office trailer.

01:51.524 --> 01:53.874
Your instructor will show you where at your site.

01:54.996 --> 01:57.721
Miners can choose a representative of miners.

01:57.721 --> 02:00.421
Two or more miners can designate one,

02:00.421 --> 02:03.133
and it's filed with MSHA under Part 40.

02:03.133 --> 02:06.008
The representative can accompany MSHA inspectors

02:06.008 --> 02:08.783
on inspections, can request inspections,

02:08.783 --> 02:11.933
and receives copies of certain records and notices.

02:11.933 --> 02:14.271
The representative's role is to speak for miners

02:14.271 --> 02:17.483
on safety and health. Right now, no Allen site

02:17.483 --> 02:19.921
has a designated miners' representative,

02:19.921 --> 02:22.321
but you have the right to designate one.

02:23.466 --> 02:26.004
You have the right to report hazards to Allen or

02:26.004 --> 02:30.004
to MSHA, to request an MSHA inspection if you believe

02:30.004 --> 02:32.441
there's a violation or imminent danger,

02:32.441 --> 02:34.929
to receive the training required by law,

02:34.929 --> 02:37.979
and to be protected from discrimination or retaliation

02:37.979 --> 02:40.591
for exercising these rights. If you think you've

02:40.591 --> 02:43.179
been retaliated against, you can file a complaint

02:43.179 --> 02:45.604
with MSHA within 60 days.

02:46.728 --> 02:49.503
At Allen: if you see a hazard, warn the people

02:49.503 --> 02:51.778
around you and tell your supervisor.

02:51.778 --> 02:54.478
Any hazard can be reported by just telling them.

02:54.478 --> 02:57.590
Equipment hazards and defects also go on your pre-trip

02:57.590 --> 03:00.865
inspection list or in the app. Supervisors write

03:00.865 --> 03:03.203
hazards on their daily inspection sheets,

03:03.203 --> 03:05.853
and you can also report a hazard as an observation

03:05.853 --> 03:09.065
in the HCSS app, which goes to upper management.

03:09.065 --> 03:11.915
Allen's rules are in the Quarry Safety Policies.

03:11.915 --> 03:14.490
If a hazard isn't fixed, take it to the Safety

03:14.490 --> 03:16.828
Manager, and you always have the right to go to

03:16.828 --> 03:17.965
MSHA.

03:19.111 --> 03:22.148
The miner comes first. Allen is responsible,

03:22.148 --> 03:24.673
and you help. Know your chain of command and your

03:24.673 --> 03:27.623
representative. You can report, request,

03:27.623 --> 03:28.823
and be protected.

03:29.940 --> 03:33.102
Remember: your site's plans and procedures always

03:33.102 --> 03:34.603
override this video.
